🧠 Overview of the A Mental Health Clinic Project

A Mental Health Clinic is a specialized project dedicated to providing comprehensive mental health services. It aims to create a safe, supportive, and confidential environment to assist individuals facing psychological stress, mood disorders, anxiety, depression, and behavioral or social challenges.

The clinic works to promote awareness about the importance of mental health and to help reduce the social stigma associated with seeking psychological support. It offers individual and group therapy sessions based on modern, evidence-based approaches, delivered under the supervision of a team of highly qualified professionals in psychotherapy and family counseling.

Services Provided

   Individual Psychotherapy Sessions
   Group Therapy Sessions
   Family and Marital Counseling
   Behavior Modification Programs for Children and Adolescents
   Awareness Workshops and Training Courses.

